Subject: A bytecode binds to a compiled function only if no other live bytecode holds it

What this does
  - `JSRuntime` gains `aot_bound`, a byte per unit index, set while a live bytecode is bound to that compiled function.
  - `js_aot_bind` leaves a second live bytecode of the same unit index unbound (it runs in the interpreter); a rebind of
    a bound bytecode clears its own slot first, and an allocation failure of the table leaves it unbound.
  - The bytecode finalizer clears the slot after the register PIC is freed, and `JS_FreeRuntime` frees the table.

Why we need it
  The compiled bodies keep one set of cached property facts per function, validated at entry against the bytecode's cache
  table. Two live bytecodes with the same code (the same source compiled twice) would share that set. With one live
  instance per unit index, an inline body entered through a callee guard (`aot_fn` equals the function's entry) is
  always the instance whose facts are cached, and the entry no longer compares the bytecode's identity. Freeing a
  bytecode resets every entry of its register PIC, each of which moves `aot_pic_epoch`, before the slot is cleared, so a
  bytecode bound to the index afterwards sees the epoch already moved.

Functions touched
  `js_aot_bind`, `js_free_function_bytecode`, `JS_FreeRuntime`; the `JSRuntime` type.

No.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -771,0 +772,4 @@
+    /* One byte per unit index: set while a live bytecode is bound to that compiled function. The
+       compiled bodies keep one set of cached facts per function, so a second live instance of the
+       same code is left unbound and runs in the interpreter. */
+    uint8_t *aot_bound;
@@ -4459,0 +4464,3 @@
+#if QJS_AOT || QJS_AOT_GEN
+    js_free_rt(rt, rt->aot_bound);
+#endif
@@ -64362,0 +64370,2 @@
+    if (b->aot_fn != NULL && b->aot_index != UINT32_MAX && b->realm->rt->aot_bound != NULL)
+        b->realm->rt->aot_bound[b->aot_index] = 0;
@@ -64389,0 +64399,5 @@
+            if (b->realm->rt->aot_bound == NULL)
+                b->realm->rt->aot_bound = js_mallocz_rt(b->realm->rt, qjs_aot_count);
+            if (b->realm->rt->aot_bound == NULL || b->realm->rt->aot_bound[mid])
+                return;         /* another live bytecode holds this function */
+            b->realm->rt->aot_bound[mid] = 1;
@@ -77632,0 +77647,4 @@
+    /* After the register PIC went (every entry reset moves aot_pic_epoch), the unit index is free for
+       another bytecode to bind. */
+    if (b->aot_fn != NULL && b->aot_index != UINT32_MAX && rt->aot_bound != NULL)
+        rt->aot_bound[b->aot_index] = 0;
